From: Solicitors for Petro Trade <litigation@petrotrade-solicitors.example> (Petro Trade Inc)
To: litigation@addax-energy.example
Date: 2022-03-31
Subject: Claim LM-2022-000140 - Defence of Petro Trade Inc

Petro Trade's Defence to the claim on the four unpaid sums is served. In summary it says:

1. Gasoil trade 7008356: the trade is admitted, but it "was concluded orally and the spot contract post-dated the agreement and did not form part of it", so clause 10 (payment and interest) is not part of it. Releases up to May 2018 were paid for "consistently with the practice", not under any spot contract.
2. The USD 460,000 is admitted as paid, but denied to be on account of any liability under the gasoil trade.
3. "At some point between November 2016 and February 2017, approximately 1,723.375MT of the gasoil ex M/T Torm Tevere was removed from China Union's tanks. ACE permitted a third party, Srimex Oil & Gas, to remove that gasoil." Addax, as pledgee, owed a non-delegable duty of care and is liable for ACE's negligence; this is pleaded as a set-off.
4. Risk and title remained with Addax, so the goods perished before risk passed (s. 7 Sale of Goods Act 1979), or the bargain was frustrated.
5. There was no acceptance of the goods, so Addax cannot sue for the price and has at most a claim in damages under s. 50 of the 1979 Act.
6. Waiver or estoppel by convention: PT would pay only as and when it took lots.
7. Term Agreement: no binding bargain was concluded on 3 January 2018, and the 20 November 2018 document is not evidence of agreed terms. There was "no certain agreement as to price"; the clause 9 premium "to be mutually agreed" is an unenforceable agreement to agree. Earlier spot terms differed "as to quality, the passing of title, the passing of risk, payment terms ... and laytime allowances". Deliveries were not made under clause 7, and clause 13 passed only risk as to condition or quality.
8. PT admits the Term products were delivered to Monrovia and that it collected the portions alleged, but "On or around January / February 2020, unknown and unauthorised parties removed the remaining gasoil ex M/T STI Beryl and mogas ex M/T Ance from the LPRC tanks."

